{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>Go down.</b> And warn them a second time — for one urges a person on before the act and returns and urges him on at the time of the act (Mekhilta)." "<b>And you shall go up, you and Aaron with you, and the priests.</b> One might think they too are with you — therefore Scripture says ״וְעָלִיתָ אַתָּה״ — say from now: you are a partition to yourself, and Aaron is a partition to himself, and the priests are a partition to themselves. Moses draws nearer than Aaron, and Aaron more than the priests, and the people — let them not breach their station at all to ascend to YHWH (ibid.)." "<b>Lest He break forth among them.</b> Even though it is pointed with hateph-qamatz, it does not depart from its root. Thus the way of every word whose vowel is full, when it comes attached with a mem prefix, the vowel changes to hateph-qamatz."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:53:13.533411143Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}